Z||000004||fiero56||07-11-2001||10:22 PM||||Had the same with another car(not Fiero). Even after a good tune-up, and driving the car on the highway before the test, it wouldn't pass. For the third try I filled the tank with 93 octane(rather than the recommended 87), and took the brand new air-filter out for the test. It passed WAY below max allowable numbers. You might want to try the same. O2 sensor is a simple easy change. I just changed the original sensor on my 177K mile '88 2.8 a few months back. Took all of 5 minutes. Hardest part was plugging in the pigtail.||||reg||1
Z||000005||AkursedX||07-11-2001||10:53 PM||||Try going to your local parts store or walmart and pic up a can of octane boost.  It'll boost regular gas up to like 104 or 107, or something like that.  It should help you pass.  Or just even try super unleaded as was mentioned in the previous thread.  Hopefully this little trick will help you out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierobaby||07-12-2001||11:27 AM||||well guys my dad thinks the car won't burn the gas hot enough because the thermostat housing is leaking....could that be the problem? I hope so cause thats an easy fix<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLOODY"> AIM: Fierobaby87<BR>http://angelfire.com/sports/sfiero </FONT><BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||6
Z||000007||fiero56||07-12-2001||09:32 PM||||I've been wrong before, but I bet that isn't the problem, unless your car is running cold. That run run the engine rich. My problem with the car referenced in previous post was the engine was running very rich. <P>A failing engine temp sensor(not gauge sensor) could also cause this problem, but I would try super unleaded and take the air-filter out to try to pass. The leaking housing should be taken care of, but I don't think it would cause you to fail.||||reg||1
